config BR2_PACKAGE_DE25_FPGA_LOAD
	bool "de25-fpga-load"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	help
	  DE25-Nano FPGA load trigger: writing a file name to
	  /sys/class/misc/de25-fpga-load/load (root only) loads
	  /lib/firmware/<name> into the fabric as a full image,
	  through the kernel's FPGA manager and the SDM. The core
	  must carry the HPS IO hash of the phase-1 in QSPI.

	  docs/de25-fpga-reconfig.md §12; source in this package.

comment "de25-fpga-load needs a Linux kernel to be built"
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
